# ---- Numbers -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spoken number words, masculine nominative by default ("viens", "divi"). 21-99 compose as
# "{tens} {units}" ("divdesmit viens"), 101-999 as "{hundreds} {rest}" ("simt divdesmit pieci");
# every hundred is listed in the form that combines ("simt", "divsimt" ... "deviņsimt"). 0 and 10-20,
# the tens and the hundreds never change; 1-9 decline and agree with their noun, by these forms
# (a compound changes its last word only: 21 = "divdesmit" + the form of "viens"):
#   (none)  masc. nom   viens divi trīs četri     f       fem. nom   viena divas trīs četras
#   m_gen   masc. gen   viena divu triju četru    f_gen   fem. gen   vienas divu triju četru
#   m_dat   masc. dat   vienam diviem trim ...    f_dat   fem. dat   vienai divām trim četrām
#   m_acc   masc. acc   vienu divus trīs četrus   f_acc   fem. acc   vienu divas trīs četras
#   m_loc   masc. loc   vienā divos trijos ...    f_loc   fem. loc   vienā divās trijās četrās
# The counted nouns below choose the right one; "{n:f}", "{n:m_acc}" ... say a bare number in that form.
