# ---- Counted nouns ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Latvian plural rule (assets/i18n), three forms in this order: zero (0, 10-20, 30, 40 ... 100,
# 110-119 ...: n%10 = 0 or n%100 = 11-19) | one (1, 21, 31 ... 101: n%10 = 1 but not 11) | other.
# The "zero" numbers never decline: in the nominative and accusative their noun is in the genitive
# plural ("desmit gājienu", "nulle kļūdu"), in the other cases in its own case ("pēc desmit gājieniem").
# "one" takes the singular: "divdesmit viens gājiens". Written: digits ("3 gājieni").
# Each noun has seven case forms; pick the one the sentence needs (examples with move / mistake):
#   {n:move}       nominative            "Šajā partijā bija tikai {n:mistake}."
#   {n:move_acc}   accusative            "Tu pieļāvi {n:mistake_acc}.", "Tu atsauci {n:move_acc}."
#   {n:move_gen}   genitive              "{n:move_gen} sērija" (piecu gājienu sērija)
#   {n:move_dat}   dative                "līdz {n:move_dat}"
#   {n:move_loc}   locative              "Mats {n:move_loc}." (divos gājienos), "uzvara {moves:move_loc}"
#   {n:move_pgen}  after pēc, no, bez, aiz, pie, pirms (genitive in the singular, dative in the
#                  plural, like every Latvian preposition): "pēc {n:move_pgen}" = pēc viena gājiena /
#                  pēc trim gājieniem
#   {n:move_pacc}  after ar, uz, par, pa, pret, caur (accusative in the singular, dative in the
#                  plural): "ar {n:mistake_pacc}" = ar vienu kļūdu / ar divām kļūdām
# "N times" is an accusative of the adverb: "{m:time_acc}" = vienu reizi / trīs reizes / desmit reižu.
# Never let a participle or an adjective agree with a counted noun (it changes with the number:
# "paņemta viena figūra", "paņemtas trīs figūras"): use an active verb ("Tu paņēmi
# {n:piece_acc}.") or a noun and a colon ("Paņemto figūru skaits: {n}.").
